{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"twoOptTour","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"improving","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tour","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Cycle","identifier":"doc:\/\/Walks\/documentation\/Walks\/Cycle","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Cycle","identifier":"doc:\/\/Walks\/documentation\/Walks\/Cycle","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">? ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdditiveArithmetic","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A move’s gain is formed as (d(a, b) + d(c, e)) − (d(a, c) + d(b, e)), and the scan stops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when no move gains anything; JGraphT forms d(a, c) + d(b, e) − d(a, b) − d(c, e) and stops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when no change is below −1e-8. The tour is JGraphT’s exactly on integers, and on floating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"weights whose sums are exactly representable (dyadic values of moderate size); otherwise"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rounding and the threshold can pick other moves, so the tours may differ."}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph is complete; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tour.vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" lists every vertex of the graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly once; no weight is NaN or infinite; the sum of any two weights fits in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"},{"type":"aside","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n²) per improving move."}]}],"style":"note"}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tour"},{"type":"text","text":" improved by 2-opt to a 2-optimal tour, by JGraphT"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TwoOptHeuristicTSP.improveTour"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s procedure: best improvement, the first move (i, j) in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row-major order on ties, until no exchange of two tour edges for two lighter ones remains."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"LEMON’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Opt2Tsp"},{"type":"text","text":" shares the name only: it takes the first improving move and restarts the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scan, which ends at a different tour. The first vertex of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tour"},{"type":"text","text":" stays first. Only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tour.vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" is read: the result uses the lightest edge of each pair, as every tour"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"does. nil below three vertices."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/twoopttour(improving:weight:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/twoOptTour(improving:weight:)"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentat